      "side": 1,
      "message": "`this.restApiService.applyFixSuggestion()` suppresses HTTP errors by default and resolves with a `Response` object (with `res.ok \u003d\u003d\u003d false`) rather than throwing an Error, unless an error callback is passed.\n\nBecause `throwingErrorCallback` is not passed as the `errFn` parameter, HTTP errors (such as 409 Conflict or 500) will not trigger the `catch` block, and `if (res?.ok)` will evaluate to false without alerting the user that the revert failed.\n\nConsider passing `throwingErrorCallback` or handling `!res?.ok` explicitly:\n```typescript\nres \u003d await this.restApiService.applyFixSuggestion(\n  this.changeNum,\n  patchNum,\n  fixSuggestion.replacements,\n  undefined,\n  throwingErrorCallback\n);\n```",
      "isAi": true,
